/*
 * Declares the AsyncType class.
 *
 * This module defines the native async type used by the Ymir semantic
 * generator. An AsyncType represents the result of an async function or async
 * lambda. Async values are non-blocking coroutines with no stack context:
 * they encapsulate suspended computation that can be resumed until completion.
 *
 * Async values:
 *   - wrap a single return type T,
 *   - borrow data iff their return type does,
 *   - derive mutability only from the async handle itself,
 *   - participate in compatibility and mutability rules as scalar types.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native::scalar::async_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native/scalar/async_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-02-24
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
